PRETABLE 3 -- #531, kill table 3: the SIBLING-PARITY repair
Written 2026-09-18 BEFORE table 3 runs; this file's mtime is the order discriminator.

*** PRETABLE.out AND PRETABLE2.out ARE NOT EDITED, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. ***
Their mtimes ARE the order proof for tables 1 and 2 (22:58:19 < 22:59:36; 23:44:37 < 23:44:43).
Editing either to add a correction would reset its mtime and DESTROY the very property it
exists to provide.  Corrections to an order-proof artifact go in the NEXT block, never in the
artifact itself.

================================================================================
THE BREACH, AND THE CAUSE IS WORTH MORE THAN THE ROW
================================================================================
The §F2 adjudication found ONE floor breach in the class closure, required by the agy seat and
independently named by grok: **`isr 28 rd val` was missing.**

The two READ arms are structurally identical -- both decline, both announce, both leave odata
at 0.  Closing the declined-VALUE cell at 0x10020 and not at 0x10028 is the #499 shape exactly:
repaired at the address the mutant used, symmetric cell left open for the next pass.

*** THE CAUSE WAS IN PRETABLE.out's OWN WORDING, AND grok DIAGNOSED IT: ***
That block listed BOTH read arms as "decline, no value to pin".

    A DECLINE HAS A VALUE, AND IT IS 0.

That framing made the miss MECHANICAL.  The enumeration asked which arms ANNOUNCE and treated a
refusal as having no observable -- when the refusal's own RETURNED VALUE is precisely the
channel M10_mirror20 travels on.  Having then added `isr 20 rd val' from the measuring seat's
prescription, nothing sent me back to the sentence that said neither arm had a value.

**THE GENERAL FORM, for the next enumeration:** when a block classifies an arm as "declines,
nothing to observe", ask what the decline RETURNS.  A refusal is not the absence of an
observable; it is an observable with a specific value, and a mutant can change it while leaving
every announce and every survival row untouched.

================================================================================
CHANNEL -- the one new row and its mutant
================================================================================
  ROW              MUTANT          OBSERVABLE THAT DIFFERS      PREDICTION
  isr 28 rd val    M11_mirror28    readback 0x5a5a vs 0x0       KILL (27/28)

  WHY NO OTHER ROW CAN SEE M11: the mutant leaves the host alive (survival rows green), leaves
  the announce firing (`kill 28 rd txt' green), and changes ONLY the value returned by a read
  that no other row reads.  That is the same blindness `isr 20 rd val' was added to remove, at
  the sibling offset.

  REGRESSION: base must read 28/28.  M10_mirror20 is NOT re-run -- it was measured at 26/27 in
  table 2 and the added row is an independent session; that claim is REASONED, and it is the
  same claim table 2 tested for M1 and found true.

================================================================================
DISPOSITIONS THE PANEL RAISED THAT ARE **NOT** IN THIS TABLE, each with its reason
================================================================================
  * F13 (the read-arm announce consumes the shared ISR latch, so an ordinary guest READ of
    0x10020 silences the write-side warnings forever).  SPLIT 2-1 among the seats that ruled --
    glm and deepseek REFINE/overturn, kimi UPHOLDs kept-and-disclosed.  NOT fixed in-round:
    it is neither a measured false pass nor a wrong record, so the stopping rule FILES it.
    The split is recorded rather than resolved by whoever wrote it up.
  * THE STRING'S TRUTH (glm and kimi, independently): "interrupt-status rewrite not
    implemented" is byte-identical across arms where the rewrite IS implemented -- 0x10020 and
    0x10028 keep their stores.  The panel audited the string's GRANULARITY (F1) and its LATCH
    (F10) and never its TRUTH.  FILED with F20.
  * THE PER-INSTANCE AXIS (kimi): P4's contract is N=1 PER DEVICE INSTANCE and the tree ships
    sgi_ip30_2, yet every row runs against one instance.  FILED.
  * WIDTH/len and POSITION/TRANSLATION: grok ruled both are NOT floor here -- no edited arm
    tests `len', and this detector claims no decode window.  Honest clause-(e) debt, and the
    contract already discloses them.
